Z||000000||Ed||02-15-2001||11:57 PM||||Here's the GT on Thunderhill Park racetrack in northern California.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thunder.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fat||02-16-2001||12:00 AM||||(Putting on my glasses)  Yes, that is a Fiero.  I always hate how race track pictures turn out.  You can never get in close enough.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||02-16-2001||12:10 AM||||You're right.  This was taken with a telephoto and its still small.  I have others, but this is the "best" action photo. I have a closer side view, but its not very dynamic. We also have some static photos of my car and others.  There was "everything" there.  Station wagons, four door sedans, a truck!  But also Ferraris, Vipers, turboed Supras and Miatas, etc.  <P>We may get some other Fieros up there in the future.  Other club members are now interested, and I had so much fun I'll probably go again. <P>Anyone interested in more photos?  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||02-16-2001||12:36 AM||||More photos please!  I can't wait to hit the track (well I mean run on it).  How'd you do on time w/ respect to the others you mentioned, namely the Ferraris?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ed||02-16-2001||01:05 AM||||There were three groups, and I wasn't on the track at the same time as the Ferraris.  However, I did pass a first generation RX7 on the straight, and kept up with a Viper on the turn after it passed me on a straight.  My instructor (this was a school, not a race) pointed this out to me which pleased me to no end.  Of course the regular sedans were easily passed, including a BMW.  <P>The car handled very well and I was very pleased with it's performance.  The only mods are a rear sway bar and plastic bushings on the front and rear bars.  Street M&S tires, stock size.     <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Untitled2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ed||02-16-2001||01:22 AM||||No, the Cushman wasn't circulating around with us!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||02-16-2001||08:47 AM||||Cool pictures.<P>Ah yes, Fiero's are tough to photograph.  In their natural habitats, they tend to be blurs to the camera lens.<P>BTW, in that last picture, is that a F..F..Fiero?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 02-16-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||Ed||02-16-2001||12:32 PM||||The black jobber in the middle is my Fiero, yes.  Oh, you mean the yellow one?  That's a F..F..Ferrari 360 Modena.  You too can have one for yourself for a mere $250,000.<P>Another amazing thing about the school was the age of the participants.  You young guys out there (I'm an old guy), all these young Silicon Valley types were there in their new Ferraris, new Vipers, new Jaguars, and turboed this and that.  I was depressed!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Tigger||02-16-2001||04:52 PM||||Wow!  If the average Fiero is lets say, about $2,500, then that's 100 Fiero's sitting there. Ouch!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>That aside, you've got a Very Nice Fiero.<P>At least you got to do some hot laps, I'd think that would make anyone's day.||||reg||14
Z||000009||Greg Piet||02-16-2001||10:58 PM||||I didnt see a roll bar/cage.<P>What was your avg speed?<P>How many cars on the track at a time?<P>What were the passing rules?||||reg||1
Z||000010||crzyone||02-16-2001||11:31 PM||||A Fiero with an LT-1 engine should turn a few heads at the racetrack.  Has anyone been at a track with a V-8 Fiero?  How did it fare?<P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ed||02-17-2001||01:28 AM||||Standard street cars were used.  We were required to wear a brain bucket (rentals available).  Roll bars were required for open cars.  For berlinettas/coupes/sedans, our windows were required to be open so they could drag us out of our burning cars.  It was cold (for California) that day and I had my heater on full blast!<P>This wasn't a race so no lap times were taken, but I did get up to over 90 mph on the straight. It looked like the big boys were probably going about 120. I had a 'vette just go roaring by. I circulated most of the track in third, with some fourth gear use on the two straights.  ('87 GT with five speed).  <P>There were three groups so I suppose about 20 cars were out in each group. <P>There were two straights where passing was allowed.  <P>Web site:  <A HREF="http://www.thunderhill.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thunderhill.com</A>   (high performance street driving school) ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Greg Piet||02-17-2001||02:39 AM||||Cool beans.<BR>Sounds similiar to the Car clinic in Pahrump NV on a road course. (there are sedctions for race ready cars and street cars)<P>Yes they are supposed to be real fun, but I have yet gotten the courage to go take my daily driver out racing in a pack and go wheel to wheel(although I bought tires for it).<P>||||reg||1
